+Autonomous Agent Design — Constrained Aegis Autopilot
+===================================================
+
+Purpose
+-------
Design notes for a constrained autonomous agent that can perform low-risk promotions, propose hardware smoke tests, and suggest operational changes while preserving human oversight and auditability.
+
+High-level goals
+- Enable faster, repeatable operations for low-risk flows (auto-promote).
+- Keep humans-in-the-loop for high-risk decisions (SME, security, billing).
+- Provide strong audit trails, rollback, and alerting.
+
+Architecture
+- Controller (autopilot_runner): scans signed evidence, enforces policy, triggers promotions (repo_dispatch) and writes audit log.
+- Agent workers: ephemeral runners that can provision ephemeral test environments (optional, requires cloud creds).
+- Governance service: KMS signing, evidence index, proof monitor and SME issue generator.
+- Human ops UI: GitHub issues and PRs for manual approval, dashboarding for audit.
+
+Safety & guardrails
+- Only auto-promote when evidence is signed, metrics meet thresholds, and cost estimate is below policy.
+- All auto-promotions create an audit issue and write audit record to append-only store (S3 or secure PVC).
+- Auto-promotions are reversible: registry stores previous model and promotion event id; rollback automation is provided.
+- In case of anomaly/rollback, an incident ticket is created and group notified.
+
+Rollback & emergency
+- One-click rollback: promotion event metadata contains registry ref and commit; automation can revert to prior model.
+- Emergency kill-switch: maintain a "autopilot-enabled" flag (GitHub secret or Vault) that can disable autopilot immediately.
+
+Security & secrets
+- Agent uses short-lived OIDC token for any cloud operations; KMS keys used for signing; do not embed credentials.
+- Langflow and any UI endpoints are behind OAuth2 + egress proxy.
+
+Operational considerations
+- Establish SLOs for auto-promoted models (monitoring & alerting).
+- Quarterly review of autopilot policy thresholds.
+- A clear SLA for auto-promotion rollback and human acknowledgement.
+
